course: dictionary
lesson: 7551
title: Slang and chatty words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to friendly, everyday talk rather than to school writing. «Preggers» is slang, a short, chatty way of saying pregnant. You might hear it between friends or in gossip, and it means a woman is going to have a baby.
explain: Slang shows the mood of a conversation. Because «preggers» sounds light and informal, you would not use it in a school report or a letter to the headteacher. There you would write the full word, pregnant.
explain: Context helps you spot the meaning. The word is only used after be, as in «She is preggers.» Swap in pregnant. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. The dictionary says it is mainly British slang and is also used in Australia.
fact: «Preggers» is an adjective, and it is only used after the word be, as in «She is preggers.»
fact: «Preggers» means pregnant: a woman who is going to have a baby.
fact: «Preggers» is slang, so it is informal and chatty.
fact: It is mainly used in the UK, and also in Australia.
fact: In formal writing, use the full word pregnant.
exercise: Aunt Maya tells her friend, «I'm preggers!» What does preggers mean? | Feeling sick from a cold | *Going to have a baby | Moving to a new house | Going on a long holiday
exercise: Which sentence uses preggers correctly? | *Our neighbour is preggers, and she is due in the spring. | The preggers box was full of toys. | Preggers the dog ran across the park. | I preggers my bike to school.
exercise: Why would a teacher prefer the word pregnant in a school report? | Preggers means hungry, so it would confuse the reader | Pregnant is a shorter word | *Preggers is too chatty for formal writing, and pregnant is the full word | Preggers is only used in Scotland
test: Sam writes, «Mum is preggers.» Swap in another word to check the meaning. Which word fits best? | *Pregnant | Happy | Tired | Hungry
test: Which word is the informal, chatty slang for pregnant? | Parent | Pregnancy | *Preggers | Expecting a parcel
exam: Which sentence uses preggers in the right chatty way? | «The preggers committee met on Tuesday to vote.» | *«My sister is preggers, and she's so excited about the baby.» | «The preggers report was sent to the head.» | «We walked preggers through the park.»
